--- !u!114 &1725190495
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1725190494}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 77589506281b3198cb244fd8ac152fe4, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Gridlock.Runtime::Gridlock.Guide.BankerTour
  steps:
  - id: banker_welcome
    title: Welcome to Banker mode
    text: Welcome to Banker mode. Here you stop deadlocks before they can happen,
      like a careful banker who only lends money when every loan can still be paid
      back.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b7dea66f79f87277ba47cc6e8db712f3, type: 3}
  - id: banker_fleets
    title: Fleets and zones
    text: 'Each coloured fleet is a process. The two rows of bays are two types of
      resource: zone N in the north, and zone S in the south.'
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1742edb20a21e8e5b810bfc0959b5fa4, type: 3}
  - id: banker_alloc
    title: Allocation
    text: Cars parked in bays show what a fleet holds right now. That is its allocation.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 32e6d3ebcb6f092f5871b9a8cf117ce7, type: 3}
  - id: banker_need
    title: Need
    text: Cars waiting on the street show what the fleet may still ask for, up to
      the maximum it declared. That is its need.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 40ef5ca8441b07b07bed7e355eab69e2, type: 3}
  - id: banker_request
    title: Request and available
    text: The cars at the gate are a new request. Fleet A wants one more bay in zone
      N. The empty bays are what is still available.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: af70fca4510eb5edb95458cd657af339, type: 3}
  - id: banker_safety
    title: The safety check
    text: 'Before saying yes, the banker imagines granting the request. Then it checks:
      could every fleet still finish, one after another, using the free bays plus
      the bays each finished fleet gives back? If such an order exists, the state
      is safe, and the request can be granted.'
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e85b3b57322d329eeb943ea7d278abfd, type: 3}
  - id: banker_turn
    title: Your turn
    text: Your turn. Look at the table, then press Grant or Deny.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1964d4731983800c79736c0ad4f4e4ba, type: 3}
  - id: banker_hint
    title: Your turn
    text: Here is a hint. After granting, fleet A needs only one more bay in zone
      S, and one is free. So fleet A can finish first.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ad1e2d0927af7eebcb146ca6c420e1d8, type: 3}
  - id: banker_right
    title: Safe, well done
    text: Well done. After granting, fleet A can finish and return its bays, then
      B, then C, then D. A safe order exists, so granting was right. Watch the fleets
      light up in that order.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c129df1ae7597a0aca5b8f652fda3983, type: 3}
  - id: banker_wrong
    title: It was safe
    text: Not quite. Granting was safe. After granting, fleet A can finish and return
      its bays, then B, C and D. Denying only made fleet A wait for nothing. Watch
      the fleets light up in the safe order.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 278418e92073195d7be6b705b9020b46, type: 3}
  - id: banker_outro
    title: What comes next
    text: 'The next levels teach the other rules: asking for more than the declared
      maximum, not enough free bays, and requests that fit but are unsafe. Then try
      challenge mode against the clock. Press Next when you are ready.'
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: de4560b885e227507aa5d08615487d3f, type: 3}
  marker: {fileID: 244452611}
  desktopScreen: {fileID: 875031123}
  xrScreen: {fileID: 776280527}
  xrMode: {fileID: 1230363085}
  desktopCamera: {fileID: 1228788499}
  game: {fileID: 902228778}
  lot: {fileID: 902228779}
  decideWaitSeconds: 18
